      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The file has many unused data provider methods and dense, unformatted data. I'll improve understandability by:\n1. Removing all unused data provider methods (not referenced by any `@MethodSource` in this file)\n2. Removing all unused imports\n3. Reformatting `data_badDates()` with grouped, commented entriesThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all seven unused data provider methods and their associated imports, then reformats `data_badDates()` with grouped entries and inline comments that explain the category of each invalid date (bad month values, invalid days for 31-day months, February in leap vs. non-leap Julian years, and 30-day months), making the test's intent immediately clear."
